Surround each side of the `extends` keyword with square brackets. Typically, distributivity is the desired behavior. To avoid that behavior, you can surround each side of the `extends` keyword with square brackets.

Example from the docs:


```ts
type ToArray<Type> = Type extends any ? Type[] : never;
```


This distributive version applies the conditional type to each member of that union, so `ToArray<string | number>` becomes `string[] | number[]`.

