`Omit<Type, Keys>` builds a new type by taking all properties from `Type` and removing the ones listed in `Keys`. `Keys` can be a single string literal or a union of string literals.

```ts
interface Todo {
  title: string;
  description: string;
  completed: boolean;
  createdAt: number;
}

type TodoPreview = Omit<Todo, "description">;
// { title: string; completed: boolean; createdAt: number }

type TodoInfo = Omit<Todo, "completed" | "createdAt">;
// { title: string; description: string }
```

It's the opposite of `Pick`, which keeps only the listed keys. Under the hood it's roughly `Pick<T, Exclude<keyof T, K>>`.

