The search results point to TypeScript 5.2 as the version that covers `using` declarations, but they don't say outright which version added them. The relevant page is titled "TypeScript 5.2 > using Declarations and Explicit Resource Management," which suggests 5.2, though that is an inference from the title.

**What they are for:**

- `using` declarations are part of the Stage 3 Explicit Resource Management proposal. A `using` declaration is much like a `const` declaration, except that it couples the lifetime of the value bound to the declaration with the scope of the variable.
