answers.text:
Error TS2540 is the compiler's "Cannot assign to '...' because it is a read-only property" error. It appears when you try to assign to a property marked `readonly`.

- **Class fields:** The `readonly` modifier prevents assignments to the field outside of the constructor. Assigning to it elsewhere, such as in a method or on an instance, triggers TS2540.
- **Interface/object properties:** A property marked `readonly` can't be written to during type-checking, though this doesn't change any behavior at runtime.
- **Readonly tuples:** Writing to any property of a `readonly` tuple isn't allowed.
- **`Readonly<Type>`:** This utility sets all properties of `Type` to `readonly`, so the properties of the constructed type cannot be reassigned.

Example from the docs:

```ts
interface SomeType {
  readonly prop: string;
}

function doSomething(obj: SomeType) {
  obj.prop = "hello";
}
```

This produces: Error TS2540 on `obj.prop = "hello";`: Cannot assign to 'prop' because it is a read-only property.

Note that `readonly` doesn't necessarily mean a value is totally immutable. It just means the property itself can't be re-written to. So you can still modify the internals of an object held in a readonly property, but you can't reassign the property itself.

